From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 14:44:39 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 22/22] libcameraservice: write HAL1 recording frames into
 Exynos encoder buffers

In buffer-queue video mode CameraClient copies each YUV recording frame
into a buffer of the video target, locked with lockYCbCr(). The Samsung
Exynos gralloc hands the video encoder HAL_PIXEL_FORMAT_EXYNOS_YCrCb_420_SP_M
(0x11d) buffers, two ion buffers with the Y and the interleaved Cr/Cb
plane, and its lock_ycbcr() refuses that format, so every frame was
dropped and the encoder got nothing.

When the lock fails, recognise such a buffer by its private_handle_t
(magic, format, size) and write the NV21 frame through the two planes'
ion fds at the buffer's stride, mapping them for the copy only. Any
other buffer is still dropped. The writer is a separate file so a host
test can build it: it parses a real handle layout, rejects other
handles, writes rows at the stride and fails cleanly.

Test: ExynosVideoBufferTest on the host, 4 tests pass; camcycle on
the SM-T520, 100 cycles with a 2 s recording per camera each.

Change-Id: Idbc66436c5038c895c50d2d27757ec61322fdd91
Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
